    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0395" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1950v06/pg381"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.00/7–1750: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Strong</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-07-17T16:00:00+09:00">July 17, 1950—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>74. Chen Tai-chu of FonOff this morning asked
                    as urgent question whether Nationalist artillery on Chinmen was entitled to
                    shell Chinese Communist batteries on mainland when latter initiated firing
                    against Chinmen.</p>
                <p>I stated this was another question which undoubtedly would have to be considered
                    with wide range of matters now being worked on in Washington.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d211-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Department pass ComSeventhFlt.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Strong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d211-f1" n="1" xml:id="d211-f1-content">
                <p>The Department sent the following reply in telegram 56, July 21, to Taipei:</p>
                <p>“Urrtel 74, July 17. Since such operations by NAT garrison Chinmen wld appear to
                    be defensive in character, it is considered that counteraction by NAT artillery
                    is legitimate when mainland batteries initiate action. Pls inform FonOff.” (793.00/7–1750)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
